:456,"meta":457,"navigation":458,"path":149,"seo":459,"stem":150,"__hash__":460},"docs\u002F02.platform\u002F01.architecture.md",{"type":231,"value":232,"toc":446},"minimark",[233,237,241,245,274,278,354,358,361,372,379,384,406,439,442],[234,235,25],"h2",{"id":236},"overview",[238,239,240],"p",{},"Kinotic OS is a full-stack application platform that handles service communication, persistence, authentication, authorization, deployment, and observability. The system is composed of several core components that work together to provide a seamless development and runtime experience.",[234,242,244],{"id":243},"core-components","Core Components",[246,247,248,256,262,268],"ul",{},[249,250,251,255],"li",{},[252,253,254],"strong",{},"Kinotic Server"," — The central platform server built on Spring Boot. Manages service registration, authentication, session management, and coordinates all platform operations.",[249,257,258,261],{},[252,259,260],{},"RPC Gateway"," — Routes remote procedure calls between clients and published services over STOMP\u002FWebSocket.",[249,263,264,267],{},[252,265,266],{},"Persistence Layer"," — Provides automatic CRUD operations for entities backed by Elasticsearch.",[249,269,270,273],{},[252,271,272],{},"Auth System"," — Handles authentication (email\u002Fpassword and OIDC). Supports three authorization hierarchies: System, Organization, and Application.",[234,275,277],{"id":276},"tech-stack","Tech Stack",[279,280,281,294],"table",{},[282,283,284],"thead",{},[285,286,287,291],"tr",{},[288,289,290],"th",{},"Component",[288,292,293],{},"Technology",[295,296,297,306,314,322,330,338,346],"tbody",{},[285,298,299,303],{},[300,301,302],"td",{},"Orchestration",[300,304,305],{},"Kubernetes",[285,307,308,311],{},[300,309,310],{},"Build Isolation",[300,312,313],{},"Firecracker VMs",[285,315,316,319],{},[300,317,318],{},"Runtime",[300,320,321],{},"Bun",[285,323,324,327],{},[300,325,326],{},"Database",[300,328,329],{},"Postgres (Hibernate Reactive)",[285,331,332,335],{},[300,333,334],{},"Search\u002FPersistence",[300,336,337],{},"Elasticsearch",[285,339,340,343],{},[300,341,342],{},"Logging",[300,344,345],{},"Grafana Loki",[285,347,348,351],{},[300,349,350],{},"Payments",[300,352,353],{},"Stripe Connect",[234,355,357],{"id":356},"communication","Communication",[238,359,360],{},"Services communicate via STOMP over WebSocket, with messages routed by CRI (Kinotic Resource Identifier). Each service, method, and event stream is addressable through a CRI, which follows the format:",[362,363,368],"pre",{"className":364,"code":366,"language":367},[365],"language-text","scheme:\u002F\u002F[scope@]resourceName[\u002Fpath][#version]\n","text",[369,370,366],"code",{"__ignoreMap":371},"",[238,373,374,375,378],{},"The RPC gateway uses CRIs to route requests to the correct service instance, apply versioning, and enforce scope-based multi-tenancy. See the ",[376,377,205],"a",{"href":206}," reference for details.",[380,381,383],"h3",{"id":382},"never-block-the-event-loop","Never block the event loop",[238,385,386,387,390,391,394,395,394,398,401,402,405],{},"A Java service published with ",[369,388,389],{},"@Publish"," is invoked on a Vert.x event loop it shares with the other services on the node, the same rule Vert.x sets for its own handlers. A method returns a ",[369,392,393],{},"Future",", ",[369,396,397],{},"CompletableFuture",[369,399,400],{},"Mono"," or ",[369,403,404],{},"Flux"," and lets the work complete off the loop; a method that is slow, because it blocks on a synchronous client, a lock or a sleep, or because it does heavy CPU work, hands that work off inside itself:",[362,407,411],{"className":408,"code":409,"language":410,"meta":371,"style":371},"language-java shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","@Override\npublic Future\u003CReport> render(String id) {\n    return vertx.executeBlocking(() -> renderer.render(id));   \u002F\u002F the loop is free while the worker runs\n}\n","java",[369,412,413,421,427,433],{"__ignoreMap":371},[414,415,418],"span",{"class":416,"line":417},"line",1,[414,419,420],{},"@Override\n",[414,422,424],{"class":416,"line":423},2,[414,425,426],{},"public Future\u003CReport> render(String id) {\n",[414,428,430],{"class":416,"line":429},3,[414,431,432],{},"    return vertx.executeBlocking(() -> renderer.render(id));   \u002F\u002F the loop is free while the worker runs\n",[414,434,436],{"class":416,"line":435},4,[414,437,438],{},"}\n",[238,440,441],{},"The platform never hands off on a service's behalf. A method that blocks stalls every service sharing its loop, and Vert.x's blocked-thread checker reports it in the log.",[443,444,445],"style",{},"html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}html.dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-dark);background: var(--shiki-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-dark-text-decoration);}",{"title":371,"searchDepth":423,"depth":423,"links":447},[448,449,450,451],{"id":236,"depth":423,"text":25},{"id":243,"depth":423,"text":244},{"id":276,"depth":423,"text":277},{"id":356,"depth":423,"text":357,"children":452},[453],{"id":382,"depth":429,"text":383},"High-level architecture of the Kinotic OS platform.","md",null,{},{"icon":151},{"title":148,"description":454},"LVvYv_3MQRd0KP7EuURGbqzxnublPPEXhVfaIKf_Pf4",[462,464],{"title":139,"path":140,"stem":141,"description":463,"icon":60,"children":-1},"Complete SQL grammar reference for migration scripts.",{"title":153,"path":154,"stem":155,"description":465,"icon":6,"children":-1},"Deploying and operating Kinotic OS in various environments.",1790213758798]